Securing Cloud Networks

Many organizations use cloud network services, requiring security analysts to secure these remote data centers in addition to on-premises networks.
Cloud networks host company data and applications, offering on-demand storage, processing power, and data analytics, similar to regular web servers.
Cloud Network Hardening

Cloud servers need proper maintenance through security hardening procedures, even though cloud service providers host them.
A key distinction in cloud network hardening is using a server baseline image to detect unverified changes, which could indicate an intrusion.
Shared Responsibility and Data Separation

Cloud service providers share security responsibilities with organizations, but organizations must still implement their own security measures.
Data and applications on a cloud network should be separated by service category, such as keeping older applications separate from newer ones, and internal functions separate from front-end applications.
